  <sharedRules>
    <rule name="Harlequin&apos;s Kiss" id="68cd-a05c-ce2d-25f6" hidden="false" page="54" publicationId="71ba-82e2-d83c-d33d">
      <description>Determine close combat hits as normal. If a hit is scored the target makes an immediate armour saving throw. If the save is failed the model is automatically killed

Against vehicles, roll a D6. On a 1-5, that is the amout of armour penetrated. On a 6, roll another D6 and add that score to the first. You can keep rolling additional D6 if you roll a 6. 
If you penetrate the armour roll a D6:
1: One random crewmember is killed
2-4: Roll a D6 for each crew, 1-3 nothing happens, 4-6 they are killed
5: Roll a D6 for each crew, 1 nothing happens, 2-6 they are killed
6: All crew are killed</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Banshee Mask" id="913f-bd3f-e0e5-fed1" hidden="false" page="54" publicationId="71ba-82e2-d83c-d33d">
      <description>Target may not fire Overwatch at the charging Banshee warrior. During the first round of combat the target rolls no attack dice. 
The mask is only effective when the Howling Banshee charges.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Mandiblaster" id="70df-5bc1-e2fb-9f57" hidden="false" page="55" publicationId="71ba-82e2-d83c-d33d">
      <description>The Mandiblaster automatically shoots before the combat proper is worked out in the exact same way shooting is done. If a hit is scored, roll a D6. If the score is equal to or more than the target&apos;s Toughness 1 wound is sustained if their armour save is failed.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Death Spinner" id="3916-a52b-ce0e-6b99" hidden="false" page="57" publicationId="71ba-82e2-d83c-d33d">
      <description>Uses a flame template. 
Roll a D6. If the number is higher than the target(s) Initiative then they are hit. For models fully under the template add +1 to the roll. A 6 is always a pass (or a 5+ if fully under).
If the target avoids the shot, they are moved to the edge of the template.
Any model hit by the Death Spinner is automatically slain unless it can make a successful armour save with -2 modifier. 
See Eldar Codex Pg. 58 for full rules and for use againt Vehicles</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Laser Lance" id="db2f-0529-f645-b2b4" hidden="false" page="58" publicationId="71ba-82e2-d83c-d33d">
      <description>Can be used in close combat when making a hit and run attack or when charging. Cannot be used otherwise in close combat.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Pack Grenade Launcher" id="d9ff-4816-b85c-8331" hidden="false" page="59" publicationId="71ba-82e2-d83c-d33d">
      <description>Can be fired in addition to a hand-held weapon, allowing the model to fire twice in the same turn. May not load with grenades during the battle.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Swooping Hawk Grenade Pack" id="2fbf-e7c7-5923-f235" hidden="false" page="59" publicationId="71ba-82e2-d83c-d33d">
      <description>Can drop a grenade while in flight onto any model directly underneath their flight path
Roll to hit and scatter as normal. Does not prevent firing weapon, but cannot also throw a grenade</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Wraithcannon" id="4b6f-195f-e5ee-b199" hidden="false" page="60" publicationId="71ba-82e2-d83c-d33d">
      <description>Roll to hit as normal with any modifiers needed. If the target is a vehicle or buliding it penetrates the armour automatically. Any other target must take a Distort test on a D6:
1-3: The target is destroyed regardless of its armour save and how many wounds it has
4-6: The target is unharmed but is moved 2D6&quot; in a random direction</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Special Shrieker Ammo" id="2286-fa23-4342-f6b4" hidden="false" page="61" publicationId="71ba-82e2-d83c-d33d">
      <description>Decide if using standard ammo or special shrieker ammo before firing.
Shrieker ammo can only affect living creatures and has no effect on vehicles. If a target is hit make any saving throw with a -3 modifier.
If the save is failed the target is affected by the ammo. Roll 2D6 during the targets movement phase, this is how far the victim moves in a random direction even if it would cause it to leave coherency. If the 2D6 roll is a 7 or any double number, the victim explodes. 
Place a 1&quot; radius area effect marker over the explodiung victim: any target within the area automatically takes a single Strength 3 hit with 1 damage.
If the victim does not explode during his first turn of random movement, roll the 2D6 again on their next movement phase until they either leave the board or explode. They may do nothing else.
Any squad which has one or more of its members within 2&quot; of a shrieker victim at the start of their movement phase must take a Break test. This applies to troops on either side.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Swooping Hawk Wings" id="2459-113d-e1cf-283c" hidden="false" page="65" publicationId="71ba-82e2-d83c-d33d">
      <description>Work like regular Jump Packs with the following changes:
Must move in a straight line between 6&quot; and 36&quot;. No penalty for tall obstacles
No roll is made for scatter on landing but cannot land within 1&quot; of any cover, building, vehicle, obstacle, or other model. When leaping into close combat may move within 1&quot; of the enemy but still not within 1&quot; of other objects as above. When charging do not receive the extra 4&quot; move that ordinary jump packs get.
Shots fired at Swooping Hawks suffer -1 to hit regardless of distance moved.

At the start of any Movement phase a Swooping Hawk squad may leave the battlefield and are removed from the table
Models may fly away from close combat in this way without incurring any blows against them
Cannot drop grenades while off the table
May land again in the following turn anywhere on the battlefield including into close combat if desired. It may not make any other movement that turn. Can shoot as normal but cannot use grenades. If they land in close combat they count as +1 WS for charging</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Avatar - Commander" id="d8af-fa88-6049-fc43" hidden="false" page="22" publicationId="71ba-82e2-d83c-d33d">
      <description>If you have an Avatar in your army he is always the commander</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Special Invulnerabilities" id="7377-2d6d-fdef-7fbd" hidden="false" page="22" publicationId="71ba-82e2-d83c-d33d">
      <description>Melta weapons, plasma weapons, flame weapons and equivalent grenade and missile types cannot harm the Avatar in any way.
Not affected by gas weapons, poisons, virus, or blinding attacks (such as photon). 

Cannot be affected by psychology in any form and will automatically pass any Leadership-based test he is called upon to take. Can never be Broken and never needs to take a Break Test. Does not count as a &quot;living&quot; model.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Dragon Cavalry" id="95f5-24ee-a5b6-2e3f" hidden="false" page="30" publicationId="71ba-82e2-d83c-d33d">
      <description>A cavalry model is treated as a single model, and if the rider is slain the entire model is removed.
Cavalry models use the rider&apos;s Leadership characteristic value for all tests that require it.
For Movement the Mount&apos;s characteristic is used. 
When the cavalry model is attacked the rider&apos;s Toughness and Wounds characteristics are used. 
Dragon Knights gain +3 to their save
In close combat the rider of a cavalry mount adds the steeds Attack characteristic to his own.

See pg. 17 of 40k Rulebook for more clarifications</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Eldar Jetibke Damage Table" id="9daa-fcbb-5d9e-d47d" hidden="false" page="datafax" publicationId="71ba-82e2-d83c-d33d">
      <description>1-2: Eldar Rider
3-6: Jetbike
See datafax for damage table</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Eldar Vyper Damage Table" id="4a95-0174-8312-132c" hidden="false" page="datafax" publicationId="71ba-82e2-d83c-d33d">
      <description>1-3: Eldar Crew*
4-6: Vyper
*Hit crew closest to the attacker
See datafax for damage table</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Scatter Laser" id="226a-e11d-d703-68b2" hidden="false" page="63" publicationId="71ba-82e2-d83c-d33d">
      <description>The scatter laser nay fire up to 6 shots during its shooting phase. Each shot may be fired at a different target if the player wants, but the 2nd and any further targets must be within 6&quot; of the first target. Declare all shots before you roll dice to hit.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Eldar Dreadnought Damage Table" id="9252-0fe1-55e3-2fc4" hidden="false" page="datafax" publicationId="71ba-82e2-d83c-d33d">
      <description>1-2: Legs
3: Left Arm
4: Right Arm
5-6: Head
See datafax for full damage results</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Distortion Weapon" id="0b04-92fe-9c9a-e465" hidden="false" page="62" publicationId="71ba-82e2-d83c-d33d">
      <description>1: Place 2&quot; radius Distrot Area template over the intended target
2: Roll scatter dice. A hit means the template remains where it is. If you roll an arrow move the template D6&quot; in the direction indicated
3: Roll another scatter dice and repeat step 2

The final position of the template indicates where the cannon hits and all targets wholly in the area are hit automatically. Partial models are hit on a 4+. Each hit location on a vehicle covered is hit on a 4+
All targets that are hit must make an immediate Distort test to determine if they survive.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Distort Test" id="73cf-4e11-d4b8-e7f3" hidden="false" page="62" publicationId="71ba-82e2-d83c-d33d">
      <description>D6 roll:
1-4: Target is destroyed
5: Target is unharmed but moved physically. See Displacement Test Chart Eldar codex Pg. 63
6: Moved. The target is unharmed but moved 2D6&quot; in a random direction.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Anti-Grav platform" id="bdea-1648-e24d-ba7d" hidden="false" page="64" publicationId="71ba-82e2-d83c-d33d">
      <description>May be turned to face any direction or moved up to 4&quot; in the movement phase and requires only one of its two-man crew to move it. The weapon may not move through difficult terrain or over obstacles.
The platform-mounted weaon is considered to be a separate target from its crew. At short range an enemy may select either of the two crewman or the weapon itself as the target. Long range shots are randomised between the gun and crew. If either crewman is killed the weapon may still continue to move and fire so long as the other crewman is alive. If both crew are killed the weapon remains on the table but is effectively useless. 
Weapon has an armour value of 10, if it is penetrated the weapon is destroyed.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Vibro-Cannon" id="e2a8-32cc-72eb-c3e2" hidden="false" page="64" publicationId="71ba-82e2-d83c-d33d">
      <description>To fire the Vibro-cannon nominate any point within its range (can be the ground, a model, etc). 
Do not roll to hit, instead roll a scatter die to see if you are on target. On the roll of a hit, it does not scatter. Otherwise move it D6&quot; in the direction indicated.
Once you have established the final location, draw a line back to the weapon. Any targets along this line are hit and may suffer damage. 
Any model under the line is automatically hit. Assume the line is 1cm in width. 
Any models hit by a Vibro-cannon suffer 1 hit at a Strength equal to the target&apos;s own Toughness. 
A vehicle that is struck suffers 1 hit to the first location in the path of the beam that is touching the ground (legs, treads, etc.). Cannot hit aerial targets or skimmers.
See the armour penetration chart on Pg. 64

If a target is hit by Vibro-cannon beam a second time in the same turn, the save modifiers are doubled. In the case of vehicles, a further D6 is added to the penetration.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Eldar War Walker Damage Table" id="845d-7d40-0574-0728" hidden="false" page="datafax" publicationId="71ba-82e2-d83c-d33d">
      <description>1-2: Legs
3-4: Weapon*
5-6: Eldar/Engine**
*Weapon nearest to the attacker is hit
**Eldar is hit from front, Engine from rear
See datafax for full damage results</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Flip" id="f55d-ca63-c3cb-ac0f" hidden="false" page="28" publicationId="71ba-82e2-d83c-d33d">
      <description>Harlequin models which are already engaged in close combat at the start of their turn may &quot;flip out&quot; of combat during their movement phase. This allows models to remove themselves from the combat engagement without breaking or suffering blows from their enemy. May move their full normal move away from the opponent and may be placed facing in any direction ready to shoot as normal. May not flip from one engagement to another</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Phoenix Lord" id="7d92-d8a7-fe10-346f" hidden="false" page="92" publicationId="71ba-82e2-d83c-d33d">
      <description>All Phoenix Lords are immune to psychology and need never take a Break test. They cannot be broken by any means, and are always assumed to pass any Leaddership based test they are required to take</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Eldar Grav Tank Damage Table" id="eea8-caa4-0e58-335f" hidden="false" publicationId="71ba-82e2-d83c-d33d">
      <description>1: Grav Motor
2-4: Hull
5-6: Turret
See datafax for full damage results</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Fire Prism Grav Tank Damage Table" id="1954-94ed-4928-7046" hidden="false" publicationId="71ba-82e2-d83c-d33d">
      <description>1: Grav Motor
2-4: Hull
5-6: Turret
See datafax for full damage results</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Prism Cannon Crystal Targeting Matrix" id="5dca-59df-5072-a2b4" hidden="false">
      <description>Any shots with the prism cannon may ignore all the to hit modifiers for firing at fast moving or very fast moving targets</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Eldar Tempest Damage Table" id="c7f5-01f0-cc31-a7cb" hidden="false" publicationId="71ba-82e2-d83c-d33d">
      <description>1: Grav Engines
2-3: Hull
4: Shuriken Cannons
5-6: Main Turret
See datafax for full damage table</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
